From de704779fbab023703769514b04ad0826c016d54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wk <58632380+wkai343@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:11:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: enable Iris2 encoding with secure ARP
 allocations

Allocate per-session ARP memory in the CP_NON_PIXEL DMA context and
assign it to VMID 11 before queuing. Keep protected allocations out of
the page allocator if reclaim fails. Preserve decoder-only operation
with older device trees.

Match OEM reconstruction buffer layout, count and 128-byte stride
alignment, supply four-pipe capability and limit COMV/crop properties to
the ports accepted by Iris2 firmware. Explicitly select non-secure
sessions while keeping ARP secure.

Accept the zero-flag encoder DRAIN acknowledgement used by Iris2,
matching the OEM response handler. Otherwise CAPTURE QBUF enters the
error path and can terminate userspace before the last encoded frame.
Keep decoder, newer-platform and explicit firmware-error handling
strict.

Signed-off-by: wk <58632380+wkai343@users.noreply.github.com>
